WEBVTT

00:00:03.010 --> 00:00:03.980
Boy...

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:08.720
Are you the Fourth Progenitor that 
Lieutenant First Class Okiyama told us about?

00:00:09.790 --> 00:00:10.870
Whoa!

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:13.590
The future sight of a Sword Shaman?!

00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:15.520
Hell, it doesn't matter! Fire!

00:00:15.610 --> 00:00:16.370
Yuiri-san!

00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:17.000
I'm on it!

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:21.780
They're strong...

00:00:23.950 --> 00:00:28.470
God, my God, grant me 
the power to exact revenge.

00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:35.590
Yukki, stay back!

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:37.900
Again?!

00:02:17.420 --> 00:02:19.430
If you wish to restrain me,

00:02:19.430 --> 00:02:22.080
you need only follow the proper procedure.

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:24.950
However, I am the commander here.

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:26.910
Attack Mage Hikawa,

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:30.370
if you resist, you will all be restrained.

00:02:30.370 --> 00:02:34.380
Hmph. A mere human 
thinks he can restrain me?

00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:36.460
That's quite a good joke.

00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:40.350
This is your last warning. 
Drop your weapons and surrender.

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:44.340
There is no need for that, Hikawa Shio,

00:02:45.630 --> 00:02:48.940
because that order is void.

00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:52.610
Major Azama, you 
are hereby relieved of duty,

00:02:52.610 --> 00:02:55.020
along with the rest of the Holy War Faction.

00:02:56.060 --> 00:02:58.490
Controlling all these people 
at once through spirit threads...

00:02:59.020 --> 00:03:00.670
Kuraki Shirona?

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:05.920
Perhaps you thought you were using us, 
the Lion King Organization,

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:08.160
but we were doing the same.

00:03:08.430 --> 00:03:14.130
One of our goals in this mission was to smoke 
the Holy War Faction members out of the JSDF.

00:03:15.160 --> 00:03:16.550
I see.

00:03:16.550 --> 00:03:18.340
But regardless of the goal,

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:21.860
using a real dragon as a decoy 
was a blunder on your part.

00:03:21.860 --> 00:03:25.070
<i>Incoming! Everyone, get down!</i>

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:32.250
Lieutenant First Class Okiyama?!

00:03:32.430 --> 00:03:34.010
Don't tell me you were also...

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:43.500
Two wyverns, eh?

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:46.250
This is going to be quite fun indeed.

00:03:47.050 --> 00:03:48.110
Iblis!

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:50.080
We found out where the dragon is!

00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:52.790
Gajou-san, Kojou's there, too!

00:03:53.130 --> 00:03:56.010
Is that so? Thanks, Asagi-chan.

00:03:56.530 --> 00:03:59.250
We're going after it. Lead the way, Asagi.

00:03:59.330 --> 00:04:00.560
<i>Off we go!</i>

00:04:01.790 --> 00:04:02.820
Yuiri...

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:06.230
Don't worry. Let's just 
trust them to handle the rest.

00:04:06.460 --> 00:04:08.240
Akatsuki Gajou...

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:12.640
You did great, Shio-chan.

00:04:17.620 --> 00:04:18.530
Schneesturm Wolfin!

00:04:21.430 --> 00:04:23.960
Come, Al-Nasl Minium!

00:04:32.410 --> 00:04:34.480
Who the hell are these guys?

00:04:34.480 --> 00:04:35.980
The Holy War Faction.

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:40.260
Most of these are crude 
replicas or mere junk,

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:44.460
but they are a terrorist group that uses 
magic tools that were relics of the holy war.

00:04:44.610 --> 00:04:45.680
Magic tools?

00:04:46.390 --> 00:04:50.280
So that's what was rendering 
our magic powers useless.

00:04:54.490 --> 00:04:57.120
I will not fall at the hands of a demon!

00:04:58.140 --> 00:04:59.140
Kojou-kun!

00:05:01.060 --> 00:05:02.320
Major Azama!

00:05:05.440 --> 00:05:08.620
Good work keeping them here, 
First Lieutenant Ueyanagi.

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:09.410
Yes, sir!

00:05:11.390 --> 00:05:15.150
This is as far as you can go 
with your imperfect magic tool.

00:05:15.570 --> 00:05:17.550
I will put you out of your misery.

00:05:17.660 --> 00:05:19.890
No... But...

00:05:21.950 --> 00:05:22.880
Stop it!

00:05:23.090 --> 00:05:23.760
Silence!

00:05:25.310 --> 00:05:26.910
Yuiri!

00:05:33.240 --> 00:05:34.280
Take it easy!

00:05:40.570 --> 00:05:41.540
S-Senpai!

00:05:52.180 --> 00:05:55.640
No! Glenda, you idiot!

00:05:56.310 --> 00:05:58.920
Senpai! What are you looking at?!

00:05:58.920 --> 00:06:00.170
N-Nothing!

00:06:01.080 --> 00:06:03.020
Hold on tight!

00:06:03.020 --> 00:06:04.330
Y-Yeah...

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:08.270
But, uh... th-they're 
right up against my face...

00:06:11.830 --> 00:06:15.220
Whoa, hey! I'm gonna fall! I'm gonna fall!

00:06:15.220 --> 00:06:17.700
It's what you get for saying 
something so perverted!

00:06:20.890 --> 00:06:23.630
Seriously?!

00:06:37.680 --> 00:06:39.510
I fell and...

00:06:39.510 --> 00:06:42.960
You're awake now, um... Yuiri-san?

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:46.420
Kojou-kun? Where are we?

00:06:46.540 --> 00:06:48.400
And where's Glenda?

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:56.310
Um...

00:06:56.850 --> 00:06:59.760
This is a cabin built 
for mountain climbers, apparently.

00:07:00.350 --> 00:07:01.480
More importantly, um...

00:07:01.980 --> 00:07:04.200
If you could cover up, that'd be great.

00:07:11.840 --> 00:07:14.250
What are you doing to Yuiri-san, Senpai?

00:07:18.420 --> 00:07:21.200
I can't take my eyes off you 
for a second, can I?

00:07:21.200 --> 00:07:23.040
You're the one who took her clothes off!

00:07:23.170 --> 00:07:25.030
Can you move, Yuiri-san?

00:07:25.030 --> 00:07:27.370
I gave you first aid, 
but that was all I could do.

00:07:27.370 --> 00:07:30.070
You did? Thanks, Yukki.

00:07:30.070 --> 00:07:33.750
Yuiri, Yuiri... Does it hurt?

00:07:33.750 --> 00:07:36.790
I'm fine. Thanks, Glenda.

00:07:40.010 --> 00:07:42.450
There were some emergency 
rations in the kitchen.

00:07:42.450 --> 00:07:43.420
I'm heating them up.

00:07:43.840 --> 00:07:45.400
Let's all eat.

00:07:49.890 --> 00:07:52.370
Yuiri-san, would you like some more?

00:07:52.550 --> 00:07:53.890
Yes, thank you.

00:07:54.090 --> 00:07:57.080
Sorry to put you through so much trouble.

00:07:57.200 --> 00:07:58.170
Not at all.

00:07:58.170 --> 00:08:02.320
You've done so much 
to help Sayaka-san all these years.

00:08:03.370 --> 00:08:07.050
Yeah, Kirasaka-san was 
always fighting with Shio-chan.

00:08:07.050 --> 00:08:12.260
Oh, so you two have known each other 
since you were kids, huh?

00:08:12.390 --> 00:08:13.850
That's right.

00:08:13.850 --> 00:08:18.730
Although we were in different grades at 
school, so we didn't often talk in person.

00:08:18.780 --> 00:08:22.510
Actually, you never really talked 
to anyone at all, Yukki.

00:08:22.510 --> 00:08:23.200
Huh?

00:08:23.490 --> 00:08:25.240
You were kind of aloof,

00:08:25.240 --> 00:08:28.770
always serious and methodical, 
and you had excellent grades.

00:08:28.770 --> 00:08:31.670
You were a little scary 
during mock battles, honestly.

00:08:31.670 --> 00:08:34.810
A-Aloof? Scary?

00:08:34.810 --> 00:08:36.610
But I guess that's also why...

00:08:37.300 --> 00:08:39.580
when I heard you had 
received a Schneewalzer

00:08:39.580 --> 00:08:42.900
and had been assigned to 
observe the Fourth Progenitor,

00:08:42.900 --> 00:08:44.720
it made total sense to me.

00:08:44.720 --> 00:08:46.080
I knew it'd be you.

00:08:46.080 --> 00:08:47.640
Wow...

00:08:47.640 --> 00:08:49.850
So since you're a Sword Shaman, too,

00:08:49.850 --> 00:08:53.850
you might have moved in next 
to me instead of Himeragi, huh?

00:08:53.850 --> 00:08:54.350
Huh?!

00:08:54.480 --> 00:08:57.300
Yukki, you live next door to Kojou-kun?!

00:08:57.300 --> 00:08:59.220
Yes... It's part of the job.

00:09:00.570 --> 00:09:02.470
I... I see...

00:09:08.950 --> 00:09:12.090
Senpai, that's bad manners!

00:09:12.090 --> 00:09:13.900
I can't help it!

00:09:13.900 --> 00:09:15.890
I can barely move my right hand, remember?

00:09:15.970 --> 00:09:18.070
Oh, fine... Just give it to me.

00:09:19.220 --> 00:09:20.040
Here.

00:09:26.020 --> 00:09:27.430
Hey, this is good.

00:09:27.430 --> 00:09:30.000
It does look a little weird.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:31.480
Tastes better than it looks, though.

00:09:31.480 --> 00:09:33.750
I think you'd like this flavor, Himeragi.

00:09:35.190 --> 00:09:37.590
You're right! It's good!

00:09:37.590 --> 00:09:38.350
Right?

00:09:39.630 --> 00:09:41.180
Uh...

00:09:41.890 --> 00:09:42.640
Here.

00:09:42.640 --> 00:09:43.640
Oh, thanks.

00:09:44.310 --> 00:09:45.530
What are you, married?!

00:09:45.530 --> 00:09:46.330
What the hell?!

00:09:46.330 --> 00:09:47.370
Yuiri-san?

00:09:47.370 --> 00:09:50.170
Oh... I'm sorry! It's nothing!

00:09:50.170 --> 00:09:52.320
I just kind of felt 
like shouting a little...

00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:53.650
O-Okay...

00:09:55.800 --> 00:09:57.200
Yuiri.

00:09:57.760 --> 00:09:59.360
You like Kojou?

00:09:59.500 --> 00:10:03.160
Huh?! Wha... Where did that...

00:10:09.260 --> 00:10:10.770
I was just thinking

00:10:11.040 --> 00:10:13.850
that I could be the one 
living next to Kojou-kun

00:10:13.850 --> 00:10:16.840
and sitting where Yukki is right now.

00:10:17.440 --> 00:10:19.920
But that's all, really.

00:10:24.450 --> 00:10:26.080
Yukki, Kojou-kun...

00:10:26.510 --> 00:10:27.690
They're coming.

00:10:27.690 --> 00:10:31.070
Yes, and much sooner than I thought.

00:10:41.590 --> 00:10:45.520
Major Azama, was it? You're alone?

00:10:45.520 --> 00:10:47.700
I wanted to speak with you,

00:10:47.700 --> 00:10:51.040
Akatsuki Kojou... no, Fourth Progenitor.

00:10:51.430 --> 00:10:55.210
How do you feel about the state of this world?

00:10:56.480 --> 00:10:57.680
What do you mean?

00:10:57.800 --> 00:11:02.500
I refer to a world in which 
a single vampire like you

00:11:02.500 --> 00:11:05.870
can become a threat 
that strikes fear in the people.

00:11:05.870 --> 00:11:08.930
And you people think that's not right?

00:11:09.140 --> 00:11:10.540
Correct.

00:11:10.540 --> 00:11:14.080
The holy war fought by the Devas 
and the Sinful God Cain

00:11:14.080 --> 00:11:18.730
resulted in the laws 
of this world becoming warped.

00:11:18.840 --> 00:11:21.520
You're free to believe that if you want,

00:11:21.520 --> 00:11:23.510
but what good is it going to do now?

00:11:23.890 --> 00:11:28.120
Or do you think you can take over as 
God and change this world's laws?

00:11:28.240 --> 00:11:31.580
Certainly not. No human can become a god.

00:11:31.840 --> 00:11:35.780
But we do have the ability 
to resurrect a fallen god,

00:11:35.780 --> 00:11:38.180
whom we can then bend to our will.

00:11:39.360 --> 00:11:42.520
Glenda was left behind by Cain 
to protect the relic.

00:11:42.520 --> 00:11:44.730
She is a vessel containing the god's data.

00:11:45.120 --> 00:11:51.060
We need her in order to fight 
the Manmade Island Management Corporation.

00:11:48.680 --> 00:11:52.140
<b>Manmade Island Management Corporation</b>

00:11:51.060 --> 00:11:53.030
What does this have to do 
with Itogami Island?

00:11:53.440 --> 00:11:56.420
We only want to eradicate all demon races

00:11:56.420 --> 00:11:59.460
and return the world to its intended state.

00:11:59.460 --> 00:12:05.260
This should also prove to be good news 
for you, Fourth Progenitor.

00:12:05.260 --> 00:12:06.040
Huh?

00:12:06.240 --> 00:12:08.820
If we can rewrite the laws of the world,

00:12:08.820 --> 00:12:11.720
you will be freed 
from the curse of immortality

00:12:11.720 --> 00:12:15.760
and gain the ability to die 
as Akatsuki Kojou, the human.

00:12:16.910 --> 00:12:18.510
Appealing, is it not?

00:12:18.510 --> 00:12:23.680
As it is now, you face 
a future of eternal solitude.

00:12:25.550 --> 00:12:26.970
Senpai...

00:12:29.040 --> 00:12:30.020
What?!

00:12:30.270 --> 00:12:31.520
It's...

00:12:31.520 --> 00:12:32.520
a cargo plane?

00:12:32.660 --> 00:12:35.190
It's the JSDF Special Attack 
Mage Regiment's trump card,

00:12:35.190 --> 00:12:37.340
the AC-2 gunship.

00:12:37.520 --> 00:12:40.200
It currently belongs to us, however.

00:12:40.310 --> 00:12:43.480
You mean... you used that to make a golem?!

00:12:50.030 --> 00:12:51.920
This discussion is over.

00:12:52.170 --> 00:12:54.550
Leave Glenda and vacate this area.

00:12:55.070 --> 00:12:58.300
What you said did appeal to me a little bit.

00:12:58.700 --> 00:13:02.650
But all I see is a man who killed 
his comrades without a second thought

00:13:02.650 --> 00:13:05.000
and injured a lot of other people.

00:13:05.160 --> 00:13:08.480
I'll never give Glenda 
to a bastard like that!

00:13:08.750 --> 00:13:11.430
That's unfortunate, Fourth Progenitor.

00:13:12.960 --> 00:13:15.470
In that case, die here as a lowly demon!

00:13:16.000 --> 00:13:18.870
Come, first Familiar,

00:13:18.990 --> 00:13:20.820
Mesarthim Adamas!

00:13:25.840 --> 00:13:28.550
Rosen Chevalier Plus, boot up!

00:13:30.350 --> 00:13:31.460
Yuiri-san!

00:13:31.710 --> 00:13:35.710
I'm sorry, but I don't think 
hiding will save us from that.

00:13:35.760 --> 00:13:36.910
Yeah!

00:13:39.870 --> 00:13:41.100
Leave this to me!

00:13:42.040 --> 00:13:43.350
Schneesturm Wolfin!

00:13:47.130 --> 00:13:48.000
Yuiri-san!

00:13:51.650 --> 00:13:54.050
A Schneewalzer 
of the Lion King Organization...

00:13:54.330 --> 00:13:56.880
It can even sever the encroachment of Nod?

00:13:56.880 --> 00:13:58.560
A troublesome weapon, indeed.

00:13:58.750 --> 00:13:59.580
Nod?

00:14:00.080 --> 00:14:03.400
The realm into which 
the Sinful God Cain was banished.

00:14:03.610 --> 00:14:09.570
It is an empty world, void of all magic, 
whose god lost his omnipotence in the holy war.

00:14:09.740 --> 00:14:11.080
Now I get it.

00:14:11.520 --> 00:14:14.710
That's why our magic 
attacks haven't been working.

00:14:14.800 --> 00:14:15.920
Correct.

00:14:16.200 --> 00:14:19.850
This armor is a magic tool that allows 
me to control Nod's encroachment.

00:14:19.850 --> 00:14:25.080
As such, it will also allow me 
to purge you and any other demons!

00:14:28.760 --> 00:14:29.570
Senpai!

00:14:29.570 --> 00:14:30.560
Kojou-kun!

00:14:30.800 --> 00:14:31.980
It's no use!

00:14:31.980 --> 00:14:33.760
Himeragi, Yuiri-san...

00:14:34.420 --> 00:14:37.180
Take Glenda and get out of—

00:14:38.200 --> 00:14:39.450
No...

00:14:42.100 --> 00:14:43.540
G-Glenda?!

00:14:45.350 --> 00:14:49.020
The vessel leaped 
into Nod of her own accord?!

00:14:49.020 --> 00:14:50.000
Impossible!

00:14:53.800 --> 00:14:54.940
Where am I?

00:15:18.180 --> 00:15:19.670
<i>This is...</i>

00:15:19.990 --> 00:15:22.510
<i>Schneesturm Wolfin's divine vibrations?</i>

00:15:22.810 --> 00:15:26.960
Paper Noise was most 
likely trying to seal you,

00:15:26.960 --> 00:15:29.230
using divine vibrations.

00:15:29.760 --> 00:15:34.000
<i>She knew this would happen... 
and tried to protect me?</i>

00:15:34.400 --> 00:15:35.700
Hey!

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:36.830
Kojou!

00:15:37.730 --> 00:15:39.600
G-Glenda?

00:15:39.600 --> 00:15:41.980
I take you back.

00:15:41.980 --> 00:15:43.630
Make Yuiri happy.

00:15:44.790 --> 00:15:47.080
How can we get out of here?

00:15:47.080 --> 00:15:48.830
Do you know, Glenda?

00:15:48.830 --> 00:15:51.150
Yes. I know.

00:15:51.150 --> 00:15:53.910
I am a vessel of information.

00:15:53.910 --> 00:15:55.730
Must take... to the priestess.

00:15:55.730 --> 00:15:56.610
Priestess?

00:15:56.960 --> 00:15:59.330
I take you back.

00:15:59.560 --> 00:16:01.780
Make everyone happy.

00:16:07.380 --> 00:16:09.770
Kanase? Why...

00:16:12.570 --> 00:16:13.760
Yuuma?

00:16:16.000 --> 00:16:17.270
La Folia?

00:16:19.590 --> 00:16:20.960
Kirasaka?

00:16:21.470 --> 00:16:22.750
Glenda, are you...

00:16:23.480 --> 00:16:25.740
going back through my memories?

00:16:29.950 --> 00:16:31.500
Himeragi...

00:16:35.050 --> 00:16:37.940
Please take my blood.

00:16:41.520 --> 00:16:43.270
Wait... you're...

00:16:43.270 --> 00:16:46.980
By sucking blood, you gain 
the memories of that blood.

00:16:47.720 --> 00:16:52.240
The information within me 
will give you power...

00:16:52.240 --> 00:16:54.740
The power to fight the emptiness of Nod.

00:17:02.600 --> 00:17:03.960
Senpai...

00:17:04.820 --> 00:17:06.210
Himeragi...

00:17:06.630 --> 00:17:07.800
It's all right.

00:17:08.200 --> 00:17:10.770
Don't be afraid to touch the information.

00:17:11.160 --> 00:17:13.690
Feel me.

00:17:26.850 --> 00:17:30.050
Of course! You're...

00:17:35.220 --> 00:17:37.680
Ko...jou...

00:17:38.770 --> 00:17:41.440
I will attempt to retrieve Glenda.

00:17:41.820 --> 00:17:44.000
Do it, Lieutenant First Class Okiyama.

00:17:48.830 --> 00:17:49.700
<i>Senpai...</i>

00:17:53.540 --> 00:17:54.600
<i>It's working!</i>

00:17:54.790 --> 00:17:55.890
Give 'em one more!

00:17:56.320 --> 00:17:59.310
Reinforcing the guns truly paid off!

00:18:04.230 --> 00:18:05.740
You think your ugly fireworks

00:18:05.740 --> 00:18:08.480
are going to be of any help 
against the encroachment of Nod?

00:18:08.670 --> 00:18:10.540
Iblisveil Aziz!

00:18:12.740 --> 00:18:15.440
Impossible! How could any demon

00:18:15.440 --> 00:18:18.220
break out of Nod's barrier unassisted?!

00:18:18.220 --> 00:18:19.960
What are you so surprised about?

00:18:19.960 --> 00:18:23.380
There has already been one 
who successfully returned from Nod.

00:18:24.000 --> 00:18:26.840
Just one, a very long time ago.

00:18:26.840 --> 00:18:30.180
You don't mean... 
he consumed Cain's memories?!

00:18:30.180 --> 00:18:31.460
That can't be—

00:18:36.350 --> 00:18:37.310
Senpai!

00:18:37.310 --> 00:18:38.020
Glenda!

00:18:39.680 --> 00:18:42.880
Fourth Progenitor.. Akatsuki Kojou!

00:18:43.440 --> 00:18:45.380
Fourth Progenitor?!

00:18:45.540 --> 00:18:49.350
Why?! Why did the 
Sinful God's vessel choose you?!

00:18:49.940 --> 00:18:53.320
You, a traitor whose very soul has fallen 
to the level of a demon?!

00:18:53.520 --> 00:18:55.120
Shut the hell up, old man.

00:18:55.570 --> 00:19:00.810
Maybe you're right, 
and this world really is twisted.

00:19:00.810 --> 00:19:04.050
But if determining that to be fact 
makes you so righteous and just,

00:19:04.050 --> 00:19:06.280
then why'd you become a terrorist?

00:19:06.550 --> 00:19:08.670
It's not the world that's warped.

00:19:08.670 --> 00:19:10.020
It's you!

00:19:10.280 --> 00:19:13.860
But if you still want to go after Glenda 
in the name of what you call justice,

00:19:13.860 --> 00:19:15.980
I will stop you!

00:19:16.320 --> 00:19:19.430
From now on, this is my fight!

00:19:19.470 --> 00:19:21.560
Akatsuki Kojou!

00:19:24.220 --> 00:19:25.610
No, Senpai.

00:19:25.610 --> 00:19:27.280
This is our fight!

00:19:34.860 --> 00:19:36.120
Shit!

00:19:36.120 --> 00:19:39.840
He's letting his magic tool 
be consumed by another one!

00:19:41.230 --> 00:19:42.320
I won't allow it!

00:19:45.840 --> 00:19:48.460
Fourth Progenitor!

00:20:02.340 --> 00:20:04.990
You know, I pity you.

00:20:05.250 --> 00:20:07.940
You don't hesitate to sacrifice others, 
and even abandon your own comrades,

00:20:07.940 --> 00:20:09.840
to achieve your goals.

00:20:09.840 --> 00:20:13.240
Were you actually counting 
yourself among those sacrifices?

00:20:13.570 --> 00:20:16.200
You're way too twisted.

00:20:16.350 --> 00:20:19.060
I'm not gonna let you die.

00:20:19.060 --> 00:20:23.660
I'm gonna make you think long 
and hard about where you went wrong!

00:20:24.020 --> 00:20:26.820
Come, second Familiar,

00:20:26.820 --> 00:20:28.550
Cor Tauri Sucinum!

00:20:37.310 --> 00:20:38.460
Pulsation!

00:20:41.590 --> 00:20:42.730
Himeragi!

00:20:44.960 --> 00:20:49.060
I, Sword Shaman of the High God, as a priestess of the Lion, beseech thee...

00:20:49.060 --> 00:20:51.670
Dawn light of exorcism, spirit wolf of snowy mist...

00:20:51.670 --> 00:20:53.400
Grant me the divine might of thy steel,

00:20:53.400 --> 00:20:56.190
that I may smite a hundred evil spirits!

00:21:01.220 --> 00:21:03.660
It's over, old man!

00:21:09.420 --> 00:21:11.120
Kojou!

00:21:15.100 --> 00:21:18.000
Well, anyway, I guess it's over now.

00:21:18.000 --> 00:21:19.500
Yes, Senpai.

00:21:19.500 --> 00:21:20.560
Nope, not yet.

00:21:22.080 --> 00:21:24.400
Glad to see you're okay, Kojou.

00:21:24.400 --> 00:21:27.760
So... what's all this 
"Fourth Progenitor" business?

00:21:27.760 --> 00:21:28.640
Asagi?!

00:21:28.800 --> 00:21:31.050
Wh-What a coincidence!

00:21:34.430 --> 00:21:36.080
It's over?!

00:21:36.080 --> 00:21:37.430
What are you saying?!

00:21:37.430 --> 00:21:41.550
I was just released from my suspension 
and finally got a break to come here!

00:21:41.550 --> 00:21:43.480
I <i>finally</i> got here!

00:21:44.820 --> 00:21:46.460
Hey... Teacher?!

00:21:47.450 --> 00:21:50.020
No fair running away...

00:21:50.200 --> 00:21:54.000
Yo. Might wanna give 
the psycho behavior a rest.

00:21:54.360 --> 00:21:55.910
You're...

00:21:56.020 --> 00:21:58.660
Akatsuki Kojou's friend, um...

00:21:58.660 --> 00:22:00.350
Yaze Motoki.

00:22:00.350 --> 00:22:03.990
I followed that disaster-prone 
childhood friend of mine here, too,

00:22:03.990 --> 00:22:06.560
but it looks like we were both too late.

00:22:06.760 --> 00:22:09.510
I... I didn't exactly...

00:22:10.320 --> 00:22:12.470
Seriously, just listen, Kojou-kun!

00:22:12.470 --> 00:22:15.750
They keep telling Grandma she should 
be admitted to the hospital for tests,

00:22:15.750 --> 00:22:17.560
but she won't listen!

00:22:17.730 --> 00:22:19.380
And Gajou-kun's no better.

00:22:19.380 --> 00:22:23.650
The moment he heard they were taking him 
to Imori-chan's hospital, he tried to bolt.

00:22:23.650 --> 00:22:27.200
Don't you think they should be more willing 
to listen to their kids and grandkids?!

00:22:27.370 --> 00:22:30.330
Well, at any rate, I see you're okay now.

00:22:30.330 --> 00:22:32.860
Yeah! I'll be able to go home with you.

00:22:32.860 --> 00:22:33.780
Cool.

00:22:35.060 --> 00:22:36.880
Glad she's doing so well.

00:22:36.880 --> 00:22:37.740
Yeah.

00:22:38.110 --> 00:22:39.680
So, Kojou...

00:22:40.260 --> 00:22:41.630
When we get back to the island,

00:22:41.630 --> 00:22:44.580
you're going to tell me 
everything that's happened here,

00:22:44.580 --> 00:22:47.130
and everything you've been hiding 
from me! Every last detail!

00:22:47.250 --> 00:22:48.800
Oh, uh...

00:22:48.800 --> 00:22:51.430
By the way, Asagi... you know...

00:22:51.430 --> 00:22:52.080
What?

00:22:52.180 --> 00:22:54.160
Why are you wearing a swimsuit?

00:22:54.160 --> 00:22:56.950
I-I have my reasons...

00:22:56.950 --> 00:22:59.680
And... how long are you gonna 
keep ogling me, pervert?!

00:22:59.680 --> 00:23:03.600
I'm not ogling! You're the one 
walking around in a swimsuit!

00:23:08.880 --> 00:23:10.900
Speaking of perverts, Senpai...

00:23:12.100 --> 00:23:14.910
That new Familiar came to you

00:23:14.910 --> 00:23:17.700
because you sucked 
Glenda-san's blood, didn't it?

00:23:17.900 --> 00:23:19.960
That wasn't exactly Glenda!

00:23:19.960 --> 00:23:23.840
She traced the memories in my 
blood and... took your form...

00:23:23.840 --> 00:23:25.240
My form?

00:23:25.240 --> 00:23:29.310
So you took blood from Glenda-san 
while she looked like me?

00:23:29.310 --> 00:23:30.670
Well... yeah.

00:23:31.480 --> 00:23:35.630
But... wasn't Glenda-san naked at the time?

00:23:35.760 --> 00:23:37.200
Senpai, you didn't...

00:23:37.200 --> 00:23:39.580
Wait, no! It was still Glenda inside!

00:23:39.580 --> 00:23:41.600
But still... you saw, didn't you?

00:23:41.680 --> 00:23:42.840
Well...

00:23:43.740 --> 00:23:44.580
Yes.

00:23:46.210 --> 00:23:50.320
You really are an indecent person, Senpai!

00:23:51.130 --> 00:23:54.880
No, hang on! That was beyond 
my control... or something...

00:23:54.880 --> 00:23:56.850
I mean, it's not like I <i>wanted</i> to look!

00:23:56.850 --> 00:23:59.000
Oh, I see! You didn't want to!

00:23:59.000 --> 00:24:00.970
Why would you want to see me naked, right?

00:24:00.970 --> 00:24:02.490
Well, I mean...

00:24:02.490 --> 00:24:04.400
Gimme a break!

00:24:11.760 --> 00:24:14.220
<b>Noodle Shop Itogami</b>

00:25:11.240 --> 00:25:14.810
You were here, as well, Lord Ardeal?

00:25:14.980 --> 00:25:16.490
Well, well.

00:25:16.820 --> 00:25:19.240
The princess herself makes an appearance.

00:25:19.710 --> 00:25:22.460
Do you seek the magic tool 
of the Knight of the Sinful God?

00:25:22.980 --> 00:25:25.040
You are welcome to take it,

00:25:25.040 --> 00:25:26.970
in commemoration of our reunion.

00:25:27.440 --> 00:25:29.920
Thank you, Dimitrie Vatler.

00:25:31.610 --> 00:25:33.360
A magic tool of Nod...

00:25:33.360 --> 00:25:35.450
So it was a replica after all.

00:25:35.450 --> 00:25:37.680
It has already ceased to function.

00:25:37.930 --> 00:25:41.630
Or might it still prove useful 
if one were to analyze it?

00:25:41.630 --> 00:25:42.770
Yes, perhaps.

00:25:43.580 --> 00:25:45.730
There's one other thing I'm curious about.

00:25:46.160 --> 00:25:47.930
The Priestess of Cain?

00:25:48.110 --> 00:25:51.900
The Knight of the Sinful God seemed 
to show no interest in her.

00:25:51.900 --> 00:25:53.660
There are two possible reasons.

00:25:53.660 --> 00:25:55.760
One is that they didn't know,

00:25:55.760 --> 00:25:58.910
which would make them a rather 
sad excuse for a Holy War Faction.

00:25:58.910 --> 00:26:01.560
I'm sure we can safely say 
that is not the case.

00:26:01.920 --> 00:26:03.860
And the other possibility?

00:26:04.180 --> 00:26:06.850
There is another Priestess of Cain.

00:26:07.180 --> 00:26:08.320
It can't be...

00:26:08.930 --> 00:26:12.650
Isn't it wonderful? 
It's getting so interesting now!

00:26:12.650 --> 00:26:17.120
Chaos truly does love that island!
